{
  "id": "m08-pair-sum-count",
  "title": "Pairs With Target Sum",
  "source": {
    "name": "Original exercise; classic hashing technique"
  },
  "rating": 1100,
  "tags": [
    "hashing",
    "counting",
    "two-sum"
  ],
  "statement": "Given `n` integers and a target `k`, count the pairs of positions `(i, j)` with `i < j` such that `a[i] + a[j] = k`. Equal values at different positions are different pairs.\n\n**Input.** First line: `n` and `k`. Second line: `n` integers.\n\n**Output.** The number of such pairs.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 2500 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "|a[i]| ≤ 10^9, |k| ≤ 2·10^9",
    "the answer can be about n^2 / 2, use a 64-bit type for it in languages with fixed-width integers"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
